# Rust build artifacts
/target
/devops/tests/project/target
/modules/target
/examples/**/target/**

# Cooked shader output.
#
# Where a `build.rs` runs the `pill_assets` pipeline over a `shaders/` directory,
# the `*.wgsl` beside each `*.hlsl` are build products: a tracked copy is stale
# the moment its source is edited, and the diff it leaves is noise on every
# shader change.
#
# The rule is blanket because the cooked output is read two different ways - the
# renderer embeds its WGSL through `include_str!`, while a project example loads
# it from `res/` by path - so the directories holding it are not in one place.
#
# The exceptions are files nothing generates. `italian_brainrot` and
# `italian_brainrot_cs` have no build script and no cooker: their `.wgsl` are
# committed, loaded from `res/` as they are, and copied out of whichever project
# cooks them last. Ignoring them would let a shader edit fall out of the
# repository with nothing to regenerate it.
*.wgsl
!examples/italian_brainrot/res/shaders/*.wgsl
!examples/italian_brainrot_cs/res/shaders/*.wgsl

# Hand-written WGSL, with no `.hlsl` beside it to cook. `master_renderer_test`
# carries its own rule for its cooked output, and the matching exception for
# this file lives there - a negation here cannot reach past a deeper one.
!examples/master_renderer_test/res/shaders/unlit_fragment.wgsl

# Hot-reload runtime temp copies
modules/pill_standalone_temp/

# Captured run output. A redirected host run drops these wherever it was
# started, including the cargo workspace root; one was tracked for a while.
# A capture worth keeping goes under `local/`, which is ignored below.
*.log

# Host-generated project workspace member (created at runtime)
modules/extensions/host_project_*/
modules/extensions/host_module_*/

# Generated build scratch (shipping bundle contents, build metadata).
#
# Ignore the CONTENTS rather than the directory itself: git never descends
# into an excluded directory, so a `build/` exclusion would make the
# negations below unreachable.
**/build/*

# ...except the shipping bundle crate skeleton, which is COMMITTED as a stub.
#
# `pill_standalone` declares `pill_shipping_bundle` as an optional path
# dependency. Cargo resolves every manifest in the workspace BEFORE it
# evaluates features, so a missing directory here breaks resolution for the
# whole workspace - including plain debug builds that never enable
# `shipping`, and including `cargo run -p editor`. `optional = true`
# means "do not compile it", not "do not look for it".
#
# The committed stub is deliberately project-agnostic. A shipping build
# overwrites both files through the generator's content-based writes, so a
# stable tree shows no diff; run `git checkout -- build/pill_shipping_bundle`
# to return to the neutral stub afterwards.
!build/pill_shipping_bundle/
build/pill_shipping_bundle/*
!build/pill_shipping_bundle/Cargo.toml
!build/pill_shipping_bundle/src/
build/pill_shipping_bundle/src/*
!build/pill_shipping_bundle/src/lib.rs

# Test infrastructure
devops/tests/__pycache__/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

